WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.579 --> 00:00:02.963
(light symphonic music)

00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:05.416
- [TC] To be happy and healthy, they

00:00:05.416 --> 00:00:07.333
need to be able to run.

00:00:09.152 --> 00:00:13.492
And maybe, just maybe, this
is my role in this world

00:00:13.492 --> 00:00:15.825
is to provide that for them.

00:00:19.715 --> 00:00:22.545
My name is TC Wait, and I am a dog musher.

00:00:22.545 --> 00:00:26.212
(plucky instrumental music)

00:00:29.016 --> 00:00:31.603
Rescuing these dogs and giving them a home

00:00:31.603 --> 00:00:33.270
is really important.

00:00:34.547 --> 00:00:38.464
We have right now 23 sled
dogs on the property.

00:00:39.827 --> 00:00:44.252
We kind of have this motley
crew of scratch and dent

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:46.678
sort of dogs that have
come to us from a variety

00:00:46.678 --> 00:00:48.794
of different places.

00:00:48.794 --> 00:00:51.483
We have a group that have been rescued.

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:52.974
We've got some from a shelter.

00:00:52.974 --> 00:00:55.458
We've got some retired racing sled dogs

00:00:55.458 --> 00:00:58.166
that are living out their
golden years with us.

00:00:58.166 --> 00:01:01.779
In my mind it's a second
chance for these dogs.

00:01:01.779 --> 00:01:03.020
Are we ready to harness?

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.062
- Yeah.

00:01:04.062 --> 00:01:06.756
(piano music)
(dogs bark)

00:01:06.756 --> 00:01:09.256
- Huskies love to pull a sled.

00:01:10.187 --> 00:01:13.646
It keeps them active, it
keeps their mind focused.

00:01:13.646 --> 00:01:17.460
This is what they were bred
to do over generations,

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.289
even though they are older
or maybe they can't keep up

00:01:21.289 --> 00:01:24.272
with a race team, they
still love to do it.

00:01:24.272 --> 00:01:26.410
You don't have to be the prima ballerina

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.680
in order to enjoy dance.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.822
The way that we make this
work is we go back and forth

00:01:31.822 --> 00:01:34.225
between Colorado and Alaska.

00:01:34.225 --> 00:01:37.102
So in the summertimes, we're
down south in Colorado,

00:01:37.102 --> 00:01:40.903
and hold down jobs and
save all that we can

00:01:40.903 --> 00:01:42.870
during the summer so
that we can put it away

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.062
towards the winter.

00:01:45.062 --> 00:01:49.229
We've managed to transport 21
to 22 dogs over three thousand

00:01:51.557 --> 00:01:54.441
miles each way, twice a year.

00:01:54.441 --> 00:01:56.593
(serene instrumental music)

00:01:56.593 --> 00:01:59.578
I've got friends and family, 
they might not understand

00:01:59.578 --> 00:02:02.520
our crazy little life but they understand

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.771
that we're doing good
things for these dogs.

00:02:06.771 --> 00:02:10.938
There is nothing like
experiencing a dog team in action.

00:02:14.189 --> 00:02:18.927
You're literally dropped into
this snow globe of wilderness

00:02:18.927 --> 00:02:20.854
that you can explore

00:02:20.854 --> 00:02:24.986
and you get to do it
with your best friends.

00:02:24.986 --> 00:02:27.403
It just makes my heart sing.

